<p>I didn’t want to jinx them, but this obvious threat hanging over their head was the main reason <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/16/xcancel">I never linked only to XCancel rather than directly to tweets</a> on x.com. This sucks not just because some people don’t want to visit x.com, but because XCancel was a faster-loading website with no bullshit.</p>

<p><strong>Update:</strong> <a href="https://nitter.net/">Nitter</a>, the open source project that XCancel was an instance of, <a href="https://daringfireball.net/misc/2026/08/nitter-cease-and-desist.png">got the same cease and desist</a> and also shut down.</p>

